  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Given that, $x$ is a real number satisfying $\\frac{5 x^{2}-26 x+5}{3 x^{2}-10 x+3}    < 0,$ then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "xhPH7",
      "text": "$x    < \\frac{1}{5}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "iZB4P",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{5}    < x < 3$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "sNU29",
      "text": "$x>5$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "fUsRY",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{5}    < x < \\frac{1}{3}$ or $3 < x < 5$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have, $\\frac{5 x^{2}-26 x+5}{3 x^{2}-10 x+3}    < 0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\frac{5 x^{2}-25 x-x+5}{3 x^{2}-9 x-x+3} < 0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\frac{5 x(x-5)-1(x-5)}{3 x(x-3)-1(x-3)} < 0 \\Rightarrow \\frac{(x-5)(5 x-1)}{(x-3)(3 x-1)} < 0$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad x \\in\\left(\\frac{1}{5}, \\frac{1}{3}\\right) \\cup(3,5)$",
    "image": null
  },
